With the given image, it appears there is a painting on the left side of the room next to a toilet. Here is the Python code to retrieve this information:

```python
from Object_Detector_Tool import *

# Load the image
image = "path/to/image.png"

# Create a list of labels to detect
labels = ['abstract painting']

# Set the confidence threshold, model size, and whether to save detected object images
save_object = False

# Execute the tool and get the results
detected_objects, object_number = Object_Detector_Tool.execute(image=image, labels=labels, threshold=0.1, model_size='tiny', save_object=save_object)

detected_objects = [(label, bbox, score) for label, bbox, score in detected_objects.items() if label == 'abstract painting']

for i in detected_objects:
	inner_text = ', '.join((item[1] for item in i[2]))
	print(f"{i[0]} ({i[1]}): {inner_text}")
```

Replace "path/to/image.png" with the actual path of the image you want to analyze. Then execute the code above, and the text "abstract painting" will be printed with its bounding box and confidence score, and the position of the text will be shown in the image.
